    "warningId": "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111",
    "warningVersion": "2.0",
    "warningFurtherDetails": "A band of rain is expected to head northwards across the UK during Monday night and Tuesday morning. As it encounters colder air across the highlighted region, it is likely to turn to snow for a time, mainly affecting locations at 100-200 m altitude or higher. Any snow falling below this level will likely be temporary and quickly melt. Where snow does accumulate, depths of 1-5 cm are likely; some locations above 300-400 m could see 5-15 cm. \n\nThis may cause travel disruption on higher level routes, particularly in combination with a strong easterly wind which could also cause localised drifting. Some accretion of ice onto infrastructure such as power lines is also a possibility. Snow will gradually turn back to rain both from the south and through the morning on Tuesday, perhaps resulting in some minor disruption from surface water.",
